Changelog

0.1.1

- renamed to TabJump and updated description in manifest
- reduced slots from 0-9 to 1-9 to avoid using the Linux/Mac `Ctrl+0` shortcut
- allow opening of popup into a tab
- fix popup styling
- added mock browser for local popup development
- updated icon

0.1.2

- background.js now owns the popup view model.
- popup.js no longer duplicates BADGE_STYLES background.js is the source of that data
- popup.js now renders state.slotViews instead of calculating slot IDs, badge styles, or command names itself.
- popup receives display-ready badge text and shortcut labels from background.js
- popup receives shortened display URLs, with full URLs preserved as tooltips
- fixed the accidental CSS selector issue where all slot titles were being muted/italicized
- added viewport meta tags to popup/options/mock pages

0.1.3
- Removed configurable badge styles
- Added a roadmap note for possible future “show assigned key” badge behavior
